add libmetal Bao port: freertos/bao machine subdir

OpenAMP sits on libmetal which sits on a per-(system,machine) port. This
adds a new `freertos/bao` machine subdir under lib/system/freertos/ so
libmetal's CMake (lib/system/freertos/CMakeLists.txt) picks it up via
the existing `add_subdirectory(${PROJECT_MACHINE})` hook when our
rpmsg_console sample drives CMake with -DMACHINE=bao -DCMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=
FreeRTOS. No upstream libmetal sources are modified -- this is purely
additive (new files inside an unclaimed machine subdir).

What the Bao port provides:

  - sys.h: minimal machine port header. Pulls in metal/cpu.h, declares
           sys_irq_enable / sys_irq_disable (required by libmetal's
           freertos/sys.h pattern), nothing else.

  - sys.c: implements the machine hooks libmetal calls into:
           - sys_irq_save_disable / sys_irq_restore_enable bracket
             libmetal's atomic critical sections. Backed by the
             AARCH64-port FreeRTOS interrupt mask APIs (uxPortSet
             InterruptMask / vPortClearInterruptMask) so we cooperate
             with the scheduler instead of fighting DAIF directly.
           - sys_irq_enable / sys_irq_disable are no-ops because we
             route IRQ enable through the freertos-socfpga interrupt_spi_enable
             at libmetal_bao_init() time; libmetal's per-IRQ enable
             hook is unused on this port (the kick is a static SPI 52,
             not a dynamic device IRQ).
           - metal_machine_cache_flush / _cache_invalidate map straight
             to `dc cvac`/`dc ivac` over the dirty range followed by
             `dsb sy` -- identical primitive to resource_table.c's
             cache_clean_range() so cross-cluster shmem stays
             consistent.
           - metal_generic_default_poll() emits `wfe` so a vTaskDelay'd
             producer doesn't busy-spin when no rpmsg traffic is in
             flight.
           - metal_machine_io_mem_map() is identity (returns va) --
             Bao's stage-2 + FreeRTOS stage-1 already cover the
             shmem region (mapped Normal Cacheable WB outer-shareable),
             so libmetal doesn't need to manipulate page tables.

  - CMakeLists.txt: a single `collect(PROJECT_LIB_SOURCES sys.c)` --
                    matches the freertos/template/CMakeLists.txt format.

The machine name "bao" is intentional. It clarifies in the libmetal
build log (`-- Machine: bao`) what porting layer is actually compiled,
and it leaves "agilex5" / "socfpga" free for future ports that want a
non-hypervisor (baremetal) integration.

